  "discussion": "A moderate, medium-period north swell will produce advisory level surf along north facing shores on Big Island and Maui through tonight. Near advisory level surf is also expected along north- facing shores and some exposed eastern shores of the rest of the islands. The north swell will gradually decline later today through Wednesday. A small north- northwest swell will be possible during the weekend. Rough surf along east-facing shores will remain above seasonal average today due to elevated trade wind swell and some wrapping north swell. East shore surf is expected to be around seasonal average Tuesday through Thursday, followed by a slight increase Friday through the weekend. Mainly small background level surf will persist along south-facing shores during the next several days, with a small long-period swell possible on Friday.",
